@apiKey = {{$dotenv TEST_TRAVEL_AGENT_API_KEY}}

### Missing Authorization header — expect 401
POST http://localhost:3000/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "channel": "telegram",
  "customerId": "user-123",
  "message": "Hello, how are you?"
}

### Invalid API key — expect 401
POST http://localhost:3000/chat
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer not-a-real-key

{
  "channel": "telegram",
  "customerId": "user-123",
  "message": "Hello, how are you?"
}

### Test chat endpoint
POST http://localhost:3000/chat
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

{
  "channel": "telegram",
  "customerId": "user-123",
  "message": "Hello, how are you?"
}

### Conversation history — message 1 (tell the agent something to recall)
POST http://localhost:3000/chat
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

{
  "channel": "telegram",
  "customerId": "user-history-test",
  "message": "My name is Kirill."
}

### Conversation history — message 2 (same customerId, should recall message 1)
POST http://localhost:3000/chat
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

{
  "channel": "telegram",
ravelAgentId": "agent-001",
  "customerId": "user-history-test",
  "message": "What is my name?"
}
